berkeley-principles-4.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: P3 (S3): "perceive" is taken as what is immediately present to the mind in perceiving, i.e. the content of sensation in P3 and as what we see, hear or touch in the ordinary way, such as the house itself where perceived_by_sense is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S3) does not follow (berkeley-principles-4.logic.r1.sense1)
